.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-harness-vm-snapshot-create - Create a harness VM snapshot (disk-only with --vmstate 0)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge harness vm snapshot create <target-id> <vmid> <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a harness VM snapshot. --vmstate 1 (default) captures RAM too;
--vmstate 0 is a disk-only snapshot, which the probe and golden paths need
and which pveforge's own vm snapshot create cannot express. The name is
verified present afterward; the names current and pending are refused.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--description\fP=""
	the snapshot's description

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="kv"
	output format: "kv" or "json"

.PP
\fB--pool\fP="pveforge-harness"
	harness pool a VM must be a member of

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)

.PP
\fB--tag\fP="pveforge-harness"
	harness tag a VM must carry

.PP
\fB--vmstate\fP=1
	capture RAM state (1) or disk-only (0)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-harness-vm-snapshot(1)\fP
